  "track.coroutines.m.context.title": "Context and dispatcher: where a coroutine runs",
  "track.coroutines.m.context.overview": "A coroutine starts on Main, uses `withContext` to do heavy work on another dispatcher, then returns to Main. You change the dispatcher, try removing `withContext`, and change the example thread names to see that names can differ between resumes.",
  "track.coroutines.m.context.wrapup": "A context is a set of elements (Job, dispatcher, name...) combined with `+`; `withContext` replaces the dispatcher element and then returns the coroutine to its old context. A dispatcher decides how work is distributed; it does not guarantee a fixed thread.",
  "track.coroutines.m.context.simp.1": "There are only two places to run: Main and a pool; times are illustrative and do not describe a real dispatcher queue or thread count.",
  "track.coroutines.m.context.ctl.hint": "Pick the dispatcher for the heavy block, drop `withContext` to block Main, or change the example thread names.",
  "track.coroutines.m.context.ctl.disp": "Dispatcher for the heavy block",
