  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.launch.title": "What does the coroutine start doing?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.launch.explain": "The coroutine starts a loop of 5 units of work, about {unit} ms each (assumed).",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.launchTimeout.title": "The coroutine runs inside a timeout",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.launchTimeout.explain": "The work block is wrapped in a 250 ms timeout. When time runs out, the block is cancelled just as by `cancel()`.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.request.title": "When does the cancellation request arrive?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.request.explain": "At {stop} ms the caller calls `cancel()`. The request only marks the Job as cancelling; the coroutine has not stopped.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.timeoutFired.title": "What happens when the timeout elapses?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.timeoutFired.explain": "After {stop} ms the timeout cancels the inner block. Like `cancel()`, this is only a request: the coroutine stops when it cooperates.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.unit.title": "Work unit {i} finishes",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.unit.explain": "The coroutine completes unit {i} of {n}.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.checkOk.title": "Does it need to stop?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.checkOk.explain": "The coroutine checks for cancellation at the end of unit {i}: there is no request yet, so it goes on.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.checkThrow.title": "The coroutine stops at the check",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.checkThrow.explain": "At the check after unit {i}, `ensureActive()` sees the Job is cancelled and throws `CancellationException`. The coroutine stops.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.checkSwallow.title": "What if the cancellation exception is caught and swallowed?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.checkSwallow.explain": "At the check after unit {i} the coroutine catches `CancellationException` and does not rethrow it, so the loop carries on.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.cleanupPlain.title": "Can `finally` run suspending cleanup?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.cleanupPlain.explain": "The `finally` block runs, but a suspend call inside it is cancelled at once because the Job is cancelled: the suspending cleanup does not complete.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.cleanupNC.title": "How can `finally` do suspending cleanup?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.cleanupNC.explain": "Wrapping the cleanup in `withContext(NonCancellable)` lets it finish even though the Job is cancelled ({ms} ms assumed).",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endCancelled.title": "In what state does the coroutine end?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endCancelled.explain": "The coroutine ends cancelled; the remaining units never run.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endTimeout.title": "How does `withTimeout` report the result?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endTimeout.explain": "`withTimeout` throws `TimeoutCancellationException`, a kind of `CancellationException`, to the caller.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endNull.title": "How does `withTimeoutOrNull` report the result?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endNull.explain": "`withTimeoutOrNull` does not throw: it returns `null` to the caller, so you can fall back.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endIgnored.title": "What about code that never checks?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endIgnored.explain": "There is no check, so the coroutine runs all 5 units. When the body ends the Job is cancelled, but all the work had already been done.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endSwallowed.title": "What does swallowing the cancellation exception lead to?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endSwallowed.explain": "The coroutine runs all the remaining units despite the cancellation. The Job is still cancelled, but the work did not stop at the right time.",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endOk.title": "What if nothing cancels it?",
  "track.coroutines.m.cancel.s.endOk.explain": "No cancellation request arrived before it finished, so the coroutine completes normally.",
