  "track.coroutines.m.effects.ch.noRestart": "The running coroutine is kept",
  "track.coroutines.m.effects.co.try": "Press \"Change the key\" twice and watch \"Effect launches\"; then try \"Recompose\".",
  "track.coroutines.m.effects.co.key": "`LaunchedEffect` launches a coroutine when it enters the Composition and cancels it when it leaves; if recomposed with different keys, the existing coroutine is cancelled and the new suspend function is launched in a new coroutine. [[src:and-effects]] The [[term:launched-effect]] bridge to the Compose chapters is X2.",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.title": "Race conditions and ways to protect shared state",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.overview": "Two coroutines A and B each increment a shared counter 3 times. The right result is 6. You choose a protection strategy and an interleaving pattern for the illustration, then see whether any update is lost.",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.wrapup": "Incrementing a counter is \"read, add 1, write\": if both sides read the same value, one increment is lost. A Mutex, confinement to one thread, and an atomic structure all keep the full 6, each by a different mechanism.",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.simp.1": "The interleaving you pick is only an illustration: the result of a real race is not deterministic, and no pattern here predicts a real run.",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.ctl.hint": "Change the strategy or the interleaving; try the same pattern with different strategies.",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.ctl.strategy": "Protection",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.ctl.strategy.none": "none",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.ctl.strategy.mutex": "Mutex",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.ctl.strategy.confine": "confined to one thread",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.ctl.strategy.atomic": "AtomicInteger",
  "track.coroutines.m.race.ctl.pattern": "Interleaving (illustrative)",
